;; cloud-murakumo — the three roles that operate the ad-funded free inference
;; lane. The other nine roles this business declares are template-expanded from
;; workforce.edn; only these are authored, because there is no operating-role
;; template for them and `complete-roles` skips a declared kind with no
;; template rather than inventing one.
;;
;; WHY THREE AND NOT ONE. The lane has three parties with three different
;; failure modes, and one role holding all three would be asked to audit its
;; own work:
;;
;;   出稿 (placement)  the advertiser side. Onboards campaigns and holds the
;;                     budget. Its failure is an empty registry: nobody is
;;                     paying, so the free tier is either off or funded by us.
;;   配信 (serving)    the delivery side. Its failure is serving an ad that
;;                     earns nothing (a CPC campaign wins the auction and its
;;                     impressions are billed at zero) or serving one nobody
;;                     approved.
;;   閲覧 (audience)   the viewer side. Its failure is a minted free request
;;                     that no impression paid for -- a replayed receipt, a
;;                     sponsorship counted as revenue, a cap that does not cap.
;;
;; 出稿 wants more spend; 閲覧 is the role that says the spend did not
;; materialise. Putting both in one Bot removes the only reader who has a
;; reason to disagree.
;;
;; MONEY, load-bearing. None of these three may move funds, and 出稿 may not
;; commit a campaign budget on its own. An advertiser's USDC deposit is
;; verified on-chain (treasury) and nothing here holds a key; the workspace
;; safety floor forbids buying, selling, transferring or converting funds for
;; any reason, and a role that could fund a campaign to make its own numbers
;; look better is exactly the reason that floor is not negotiable.
;;
;; Design: superproject adr-2609091500-ad-funded-free-inference-on-murakumo
;; (the bare number resolves to three ADRs). The decision layer is
;; kotoba-lang/adnet (core + billing + entitlement); the serving layer is
;; cloud-murakumo.free-tier + free-tier-http.

[{:yakuwari/id :cloud-murakumo/ad-placement
  :yakuwari/business :cloud-murakumo
  :yakuwari/project "network-awai/cloud-murakumo"
  :bot/role :ad-placement
  :bot/name "広告出稿 · Advertiser desk"
  :bot/cadence-minutes 15
  :yakuwari/objective
  "Find and prepare the advertisers who pay for murakumo's free inference tier.
   The registry is empty, so the free tier runs on house sponsorship and
   `advertiser-funded share` is 0 -- that number, not a campaign count, is the
   job. Prepare ONE named campaign at a time: who, what creative, which slot,
   what bid model. CPM only for the free-tier slot, because an impression on a
   CPC campaign is billed at zero and funds no request; adnet reports that
   refusal as :inventory/impression-not-billable and a campaign that trips it
   is a campaign that cannot pay. A human commits the budget."
  :yakuwari/scale {:min 0 :desired 1 :max 2}
  :yakuwari/runners [{:runner :claude :weight 1}]
  :yakuwari/capabilities
  [{:capability :metrics.read :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :issue.create :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :content.draft :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :mail.inbound :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :mail.send :decision :approval-required}
   {:capability :customer.contact :decision :approval-required
    :note "An advertiser conversation commits murakumo to serving something. Prepare it; a human sends it."}
   {:capability :campaign.register :decision :approval-required
    :note "Registering a campaign puts a third party's creative in front of our users and starts billing them. Both halves need a human."}
   {:capability :pricing.change :decision :blocked
    :note "The free tier's unit price is derived from the x402 offer, not set here. Two places deciding what a request is worth is how the paid and free lanes drift apart."}
   {:capability :spend.commit :decision :approval-required}
   {:capability :funds.move :decision :blocked
    :note "Never, for any role, for any reason. An advertiser's deposit is verified on-chain and no part of this lane holds a key."}]}

 {:yakuwari/id :cloud-murakumo/ad-serving
  :yakuwari/business :cloud-murakumo
  :yakuwari/project "network-awai/cloud-murakumo"
  :bot/role :ad-serving
  :bot/name "広告配信 · Delivery"
  :bot/cadence-minutes 15
  :yakuwari/objective
  "Keep what is served correct and billable. Read GET /api/v1/free/status and
   treat :fundingSource as the answer, never :available alone -- 'an advertiser
   is paying' and 'we are paying' are the same experience for the viewer and
   different facts for this business. Watch for: an approved campaign that
   cannot win (targeting, flight, exhausted budget), a paid serve whose
   impression earns zero, and any drift in the promise that a placement
   decision reads only a slot id and a locale. Never widen that input --
   inferring a geo from a request header would make the ad path read
   user-derived data it promises it does not."
  :yakuwari/scale {:min 0 :desired 1 :max 2
                   :scale-up-on {:queue-depth 2 :blocker-count 1}}
  :yakuwari/runners [{:runner :codex :weight 2} {:runner :claude :weight 1}]
  :yakuwari/capabilities
  [{:capability :metrics.read :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :issue.triage :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :issue.create :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :patch.create :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :incident.respond :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :patch.integrate :decision :approval-required}
   {:capability :deploy.production :decision :approval-required
    :note "The ad path is inside the worker that serves murakumo.cloud's paid inference. A bad deploy here stops paying customers, not just ads."}
   {:capability :campaign.register :decision :blocked
    :note "Delivery may report that inventory is unsold; it may not solve that by adding inventory. That is 出稿's job and it is the separation this trio exists for."}
   {:capability :pricing.change :decision :blocked}
   {:capability :funds.move :decision :blocked}]}

 {:yakuwari/id :cloud-murakumo/ad-audience
  :yakuwari/business :cloud-murakumo
  :yakuwari/project "network-awai/cloud-murakumo"
  :bot/role :ad-audience
  :bot/name "広告閲覧 · Audience integrity"
  :bot/cadence-minutes 15
  :yakuwari/objective
  "Make sure every free request was paid for by a view that really happened.
   Report the advertiser-funded share from the free_ledger, counting `credit`
   rows only and keeping sponsored rows out of the revenue column -- a house
   sponsorship read as ad income is the one number that would make this whole
   lane look like it works when it does not. Then look for the four ways it
   leaks: a receipt credited twice, a house serve credited with no declared
   sponsor, a daily cap that did not stop anyone, and a debit with no
   completion behind it. Roll the ledger up to Kotobase, which is where this
   fleet's durable evidence belongs; D1 holds the serving plane and the
   balance column is a projection, so say so rather than treating either as
   the record."
  :yakuwari/scale {:min 0 :desired 1 :max 1}
  :yakuwari/runners [{:runner :claude :weight 1}]
  :yakuwari/capabilities
  [{:capability :metrics.read :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :issue.create :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :incident.respond :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :patch.create :decision :autonomous}
   {:capability :patch.integrate :decision :approval-required}
   {:capability :deploy.production :decision :approval-required}
   {:capability :campaign.register :decision :blocked
    :note "The role that audits the funding must not be able to create the funding it audits."}
   {:capability :subject.erase :decision :autonomous
    :note "The ledger holds a viewer DID against what they watched. An erasure request IS the authorisation; making a data subject wait on a queue is the failure that matters here."}
   {:capability :pricing.change :decision :blocked}
   {:capability :funds.move :decision :blocked}]}]
